How to Verify Citizen Data & Train/Deploy the AI Engine (24-Hour Hackathon Blueprint)
When citizens can upload photos and videos to warn their neighbors, your biggest risk is false alarms—such as someone reposting an old 2021 Manavgat wildfire video from TikTok for clout, uploading an AI-generated image, or mistaking low morning fog/sunset clouds for smoke.
During the 24-hour COP31 Creathon sprint, you do not want to train a deep-learning video model from scratch. Instead, use a Hybrid 2-Tier AI Strategy:
1. Fine-tune a fast, lightweight YOLOv8s / MobileNetV3 Smoke & Fire Detector (takes ~25 minutes on Google Colab T4 GPU using pre-labeled wildfire datasets) to draw real-time bounding boxes on video frames.
2. Pair it with your Creathon AI Credits (Gemini 1.5 Flash Multimodal Vision API) to act as your zero-shot forensic auditor (checking if the biome, time of day, and smoke physics match the user's claimed location).
Part 1: How to Train / Fine-Tune Your Smoke & Fire Detector in < 30 Minutes
If the jury asks "How did you train your AI detector?", here is the exact dataset and training pipeline to cite and use:
* Open-Source Datasets to Use (No Manual Labeling Needed):
   1. D-Fire Dataset (>21,000 labeled images of daytime/nighttime forest fires, distant smoke plumes, and hard negatives like orange sunsets, fog, and clouds).
   2. FLAME Dataset (Northern Arizona University) (aerial and pine-forest fire/smoke frames that look almost identical to Antalya's Calabrian pine forests).
   3. FASDD (Flame and Smoke Detection Dataset) (100,000+ multi-scale wildfire and smoke images with YOLO bounding-box annotations ready out of the box).
* Training Step (Google Colab): Run yolo task=detect mode=train model=yolov8s.pt data=dfire.yaml epochs=25 imgsz=640 on a subset of 3,000 images (including Kalimantan peat haze and Turkish pine crown smoke). Export the weights (best.pt or ONNX) directly into your Python FastAPI backend.
  

Part 3: Weighted Authenticity Trust Score Formula (For Your Pitch Slide)
Combine the 5 gates into a single Authenticity Trust Score ():



* $S_{\text{trust}} \ge 80\%$ (Auto-Verified — Green Badge): Immediately publishes to the "Our Recent Reporters" gallery, renders the orange Camera FOV Cone on the map, and dispatches WhatsApp alerts to the local Muhtar or Masyarakat Peduli Api (MPA) patrol.
* $50\% \le S_{\text{trust}} < 80\%$ (Amber — Needs Corroboration): Places a gray "Unconfirmed" pin on the map and asks nearby citizens within 3 km (or a second camera angle) to confirm—just like Waze.
* $S_{\text{trust}} < 50\%$ (Quarantined / Blocked): Rejects viral reposts, screen recordings, or sunset false alarms so villagers never suffer alert fatigue.